- # `↯/s.60.2` — `Parse.Error`
+ # `↯/s.60.2` — `Parse.Error`

- Raised when Zephyrine cannot parse a value of a registered format.
+ Lançado quando o Zephyrine não consegue analisar um valor de um formato registrado.

- ## Cause
+ ## Causa

- `Parse.Error` is a generic format-parsing error. It carries the
- `Format` being parsed, the `Position` at which the parser was
- located, and the `Issue` reported by the format-specific parser.
+ `Parse.Error` é um erro genérico de análise de formato. Ele carrega o `Format` que está sendo
+ analisado, a `Position` em que o parser se encontrava e o `Issue` relatado pelo parser
+ específico do formato.

- ## Example message
+ ## Mensagem de exemplo

=
- ```
+ ```

- [↯/s.60.2] the JSON was not valid at offset 12 because an unexpected character was found
+ [↯/s.60.2] the JSON was not valid at offset 12 because an unexpected character was found

= [↯/s.60.2] the JSON was not valid at offset 12 because an unexpected character was found
- ```
+ ```

- ## Resolution
+ ## Resolução

- Use the embedded `Position` and `Issue` to locate and correct the
- problem in the input.
+ Use a `Position` e o `Issue` embutidos para localizar e corrigir o problema na entrada.

- ## See also
+ ## Veja também

- - Source: `lib/zephyrine/src/core/zephyrine.Parse.scala`
+ - Código-fonte: `lib/zephyrine/src/core/zephyrine.Parse.scala`
